    A["Start Loop"] --> B["Compare field in structj vs structj+1"]
    B -- Yes, needs swap --> C["Create temporary struct variable"]
    C --> D["Swap entire structs"]
    B -- No --> E["Move to next pair"]
    D --> E
    E --> F["End of array?"]
    F -- No --> B
    F -- Yes --> G["Sorted!"]
```

## Implementation Plan
1. **Create a Temporary Holder**: Since you are swapping structs, you need a temporary variable of the **same struct type** to hold the data during the swap.
2. **Target the Field**: Use the dot operator (e.g., `students[j].score`) inside your `if` condition to decide when to swap.
3. **Swap the Whole Struct**: Assign the entire struct at `j` to your temporary variable, then move `j+1` into `j`, and finally move the temporary variable into `j+1`.

```c
// Assuming you have: struct Student { int score; char name[20]; };
// And an array: struct Student class[5];

if (class[j].score > class[j + 1].score) {
    // Swap the entire struct!
    struct Student temp = class[j];
    class[j] = class[j + 1];
    class[j + 1] = temp;
}
```

